 "description": "The place of a value is one unit of its last written digit, times the scale that the value takes: a scale item, or a missing scale under a heading. So values in thousands may differ by half a thousand each: 10,001 against 6,000 plus 4,000 holds, with an allowance of 1500. In millions, 12 against 7 plus 3 fails by 2000000, more than its allowance of 1500000. A value with a missing part still counts (spec 0.10, #321, #284).",
